For learning **Playwright + TypeScript** like a real-world QA Automation Engineer, I recommend building the framework in phases rather than writing everything at once. This is how automation teams usually build enterprise frameworks.

The OrangeHRM demo site is available at [OrangeHRM Demo](https://opensource-demo.orangehrmlive.com/web/index.php/auth/login?utm_source=chatgpt.com). The current demo credentials are **Admin / admin123**. ([opensource-demo.orangehrmlive.com][1])

# Phase 0 - Prerequisites

Before writing a single test:

* Install VS Code
* Install Node.js (LTS)
* Install Git
* Install Playwright
* Install TypeScript
* Install ESLint
* Install Prettier
* Install Playwright Extension for VS Code

---

# Phase 1 - Create Project

```
orangehrm-playwright-framework/
```

Initialize

```
npm init -y
```

Install Playwright

```
npm init playwright@latest
```

Choose

```
TypeScript ✔
tests folder ✔
GitHub Actions ✔
Playwright Browsers ✔
